From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 50/50] feat(gpu): add motion vector shader modifications for a
 temporal upscaler

A temporal upscaler (FSR, DLSS, XeSS) needs each pixel's motion to where
it was in the previous frame. Guest vertex shaders compute their position
from float constants and from vertex streams (instance and bone
transforms) that the title rewrites every frame, so the translator gets
the previous position by running the vertex shader's code a second time
against the previous frame's float and vertex fetch constants.

With vertex.motion_vectors, the DXBC translator emits the main loop twice:
after the normal pass it re-initializes the registers and translates the
ucode again, with float constants read from CbufferRegister::
kPreviousFloatConstants (b5) and vertex fetch constants from
kPreviousFetchConstants (b6), keeping only register and position writes.
It outputs the current and the previous host clip space positions as two
TEXCOORDs after the guest's interpolators. With pixel.motion_vectors, the
pixel shader writes the motion from the pixel to its previous position in
UV space (Y down) to SV_Target4 (kMotionVectorRenderTarget), past the
guest's color targets. Both are for RTV-path kVertex shaders without
memexport; the host renderer chooses the draws and supplies the previous
constants. The new bits are zero in existing modifications, which
translate as before.

The motion is bounded to two screens either way, and a previous position
behind the camera (W <= 0, where the division flips it onto the screen)
moves by the bound: it was not on screen. A position just in front of the
camera divides to beyond what R16G16_FLOAT holds, and an infinity or a NaN
in a temporal upscaler's motion spreads through its history.

ShaderTranslator::TranslateUcode is split out of TranslateAnalyzedShader
so that an implementation can emit the code more than once, and the DXBC
translator's main loop and position conversions become functions of their
own.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

